## 4.3 Functional Architecture: Types of Constructors in Java/C++

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    CON[Constructors] --> DC[Default No-Arg]
    CON --> PC[Parameterized]
    CON --> CC[Copy Constructor]
    CON --> PC2[Private Constructor]

    DC --> DC1[Auto-provided if none written]
    DC --> DC2[Initializes with default values]

    PC --> PC1[Accepts arguments]
    PC --> PC2[Enables flexible initialization]

    CC --> CC1[Takes same class object]
    CC --> CC2[Clones state from source]

    PC2 --> P1[Used in Singleton Pattern]
    PC2 --> P2[Restricts external instantiation]

    styleCON fill:#fff4e1,stroke:#cc6600
    styleDC fill:#e1f5ff,stroke:#0066cc
    stylePC fill:#e1ffe1,stroke:#009900
    styleCC fill:#f5e1ff,stroke:#6600cc
    stylePC2 fill:#ffe1f5,stroke:#cc0066
```

