### Q1. [KTU University Exam - Dec 2023]
**Define the Singleton design pattern. State any two real-world scenarios where it is applied.**

**Model Answer:**

> **Definition:** The Singleton design pattern is a creational pattern that ensures a class has **only one instance** and provides a **global point of access** to that instance. It is implemented by declaring a `private static` instance, a `private` constructor, and a `public static getInstance()` method.

**Two Real-World Scenarios:**
1. **Logger Classes:** In enterprise applications, a single Logger instance is used to write logs to a file. Multiple Logger instances would cause file-lock conflicts.
2. **Database Connection Pool:** A single Connection Pool manager ensures all database connections are centrally controlled, preventing resource exhaustion.
3. *(Alternate)* **Configuration Manager:** Reads `application.properties` once and provides global access to configuration values.

*(Other valid scenarios: Caches, Thread Pools, Runtime environment, Device Drivers.)*

---

### Q2. [KTU University Exam - May 2024]
**What is the Adapter design pattern? Differentiate between Object Adapter and Class Adapter.**

**Model Answer:**

> **Definition:** The Adapter pattern is a structural design pattern that **converts the interface of a class into another interface that the client expects**, allowing classes with incompatible interfaces to collaborate. It acts as a wrapper.

**Difference Table:**

| Feature | Object Adapter | Class Adapter |
|---------|---------------|---------------|
| Mechanism | Composition (HAS-A) | Inheritance (IS-A) |
| Java Support | Yes (single inheritance) | No (requires multiple inheritance) |
| Flexibility | Can adapt multiple adaptees | Tied to one parent class |
| Coupling | Loose | Tight |

