## ⚠️ KTU Examiner's Valuation Warning / Pitfall Callout

> [!WARNING]
> **Common Mistakes Where Students Lose Marks:**
>
> 1. **Forgetting `private` constructor in Singleton:** If the constructor is `public`, anyone can create new instances via `new` — **Singleton guarantee is broken.** Deduct 1-2 marks.
>
> 2. **Not using `volatile` in Double-Checked Locking:** Without `volatile`, the JVM may reorder instructions, causing a thread to see a partially-constructed object. Deduct 1 mark if missing.
>
> 3. **Confusing Adapter with Decorator:** Both are "wrappers." The **Adapter converts interfaces**, while **Decorator adds new behavior** without changing the interface. Mixing these is a common error.
>
> 4. **Writing Class Adapter in Java using `extends` twice:** Java doesn't support multiple class inheritance. Always use **composition** (Object Adapter) in Java code.
>
> 5. **Not drawing UML diagram in Part (a):** KTU 2024 Scheme Part (a) questions (7 marks) expect a **UML Class Diagram** along with code. Missing the diagram loses 1-2 marks.
>
> 6. **Using `synchronized` inside `getInstance()` without explaining why:** Just adding `synchronized` without justifying the race condition shows shallow understanding.

