### Question 1 `[KTU University Exam – May 2024, Set A]`

**What are the differences between AWT and Swing in Java?**

#### Model Answer (3 marks)

| # | AWT (`java.awt`) | Swing (`javax.swing`) |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Heavyweight** — uses native OS peers. | **Lightweight** — written in pure Java, no native peers. |
| 2 | Limited component set (`Button`, `Label`, `TextField`, `Choice`, `List`, `Canvas`). | Rich component set (`JButton`, `JLabel`, `JTable`, `JTree`, `JTabbedPane`, `JSlider`, etc.). |
| 3 | Look-and-Feel is bound to the operating system. | **Pluggable Look-and-Feel** — Metal, Nimbus, System, Motif. |
| 4 | No support for `JComponent` features like tooltips and borders. | Supports tooltips, borders, double-buffering, keyboard mnemonics. |
| 5 | Follows no MVC pattern. | Follows (modified) **MVC architecture** with a separate `Model`. |

*(3 marks allocated: 1 mark per key difference × 3 differences.)*

