## Topic Recap & Important Things to Remember

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Rapid-Revision Checklist — Swing Packages (Module 4)**

- ✅ Swing components are in the **`javax.swing`** package (note: `javax`, not `java`).
- ✅ The base class for almost all Swing components is **`javax.swing.JComponent`**.
- ✅ Top-level containers (`JFrame`, `JDialog`, `JApplet`) extend `java.awt.Window` and are **heavyweight**; all other Swing components are **lightweight**.
- ✅ **Pluggable Look-and-Feel** allows the same component to appear differently on different OSes / themes.
- ✅ **Default Layouts:** `JFrame` content pane → `BorderLayout`; `JPanel` → `FlowLayout`; `JDialog` → `BorderLayout`.
- ✅ **Delegation Event Model** has 3 parts: **Source**, **Event object**, **Listener interface**.
- ✅ **Adapter classes** (e.g., `MouseAdapter`, `KeyAdapter`, `WindowAdapter`) are abstract convenience classes with empty method bodies — used to avoid implementing all methods of a listener interface.
- ✅ **MVC** in Swing is actually a **Model–UI Delegate** variant where View + Controller are merged. Models: `TableModel`, `ListModel`, `TreeModel`, `ButtonModel`, `Document`.
- ✅ **Event Dispatch Thread (EDT):** All Swing UI updates should happen on the EDT; Swing is **not thread-safe**.
- ✅ `JOptionPane` provides 4 dialog types: `showMessageDialog`, `showInputDialog`, `showConfirmDialog`, `showOptionDialog`.
- ✅ **Container hierarchy:** `JFrame` → `JPanel` → components. Always `setVisible(true)` **after** adding components.
- ✅ `JPasswordField.getPassword()` returns **`char[]`** (not `String`) for security — clearing the array after use is best practice.
- ✅ For images, use `ImageIcon` and pass to `JLabel.setIcon()` or `JButton.setIcon()`.
- ✅ **`JTabbedPane`** = tabs, **`JSplitPane`** = resizable divider, **`JLayeredPane`** = depth layering (used in drag-and-drop).
- ✅ **Event Listeners to memorize:** `ActionListener` (1 method), `MouseListener` (5 methods → use `MouseAdapter`), `KeyListener` (3 methods → use `KeyAdapter`), `WindowListener` (7 methods → use `WindowAdapter`), `ItemListener`, `ChangeListener`, `ListSelectionListener`.
- ✅ **Border creation:** Always via `BorderFactory.createXxxBorder()` — never instantiate `Border` directly.
- ✅ **For 14-mark questions,** always include: import statements, component declarations, layout setup, listener registration, event-handling logic, `setVisible(true)`, and **error handling** where applicable.
- ✅ AWT vs Swing comparison is worth **at least 1 question per exam** — memorize the 5–8 key differences.

