### Question 1 `[KTU University Exam - Dec 2023]`
**Differentiate between `java.awt.Frame` and `javax.swing.JFrame`.**

**Model Answer**:

| Feature | `java.awt.Frame` | `javax.swing.JFrame` |
|---|---|---|
| **Package** | `java.awt` | `javax.swing` |
| **Component Type** | Heavyweight (uses OS peer) | Lightweight (rendered in Java) |
| **Pluggable Look & Feel** | Not supported | Fully supported (Metal, Nimbus, etc.) |
| **MVC Architecture** | Not followed | Follows MVC pattern |
| **Double Buffering** | Manual | Built-in automatic |
| **Content Pane** | Not separate | Has dedicated layered panes (Glass, Layered, Content, Menu) |
| **Default Layout** | `BorderLayout` | `BorderLayout` (on content pane) |
| **Performance** | Slower on cross-platform | Faster and consistent |

> [!NOTE]
> The fundamental difference: **`JFrame` is a `Frame` with extra Swing capabilities** — it is a supercharged version of AWT's Frame.

