## KTU Examiner's Valuation Warning / Pitfall Callout

> [!WARNING]
> **Top 5 Ways Students Lose Marks in JFrame Questions**
> 
> 1. **Forgetting `setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE)`** — If the program doesn't terminate properly after the window is closed, the examiner deducts 1-2 marks and may ask in viva why the JVM doesn't exit.
> 
> 2. **Wrong import statements** — Writing `import javax.swing.*;` without realizing some questions specifically test knowledge of individual class imports. Both forms are accepted, but mixing them inconsistently looks sloppy.
> 
> 3. **Adding components before setting the layout** — The order matters! Always set the layout first, then add components, then `setSize()`, then `setVisible(true)`. Reverse order can cause rendering glitches.
> 
> 4. **Confusing `Frame` and `JFrame`** — AWT's `Frame` does NOT have `setDefaultCloseOperation()` method (it uses `WindowAdapter` instead). Mixing up the two classes leads to compile-time errors.
> 
> 5. **Missing `main()` method signature** — Writing `public static void Main(String[] args)` (capital M) is a compile error. Java is case-sensitive.

